<title>RUSSIA: Quiet Russian MinFins steady, wait for New Year.</title>
<headline>Quiet Russian MinFins steady, wait for New Year.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices of Russian MinFin bonds were little changed in quiet trading on Tuesday as banks saw no news that could liven up the market before the end of the year.</p>
<p>		 tranche  Dec 17		  Dec 16</p>
<p> 1999 maturity (3)    83.70-84.00	   83.70-84.00</p>
<p> 2003 maturity (4)    59.70-60.00	   59.80-60.10</p>
<p> 2008 maturity (5)    41.70-42.00	   41.80-42.10</p>
<p> 2006 maturity (6)    47.50-47.80	   47.40-47.90</p>
<p> 2011 maturity (7)    35.35-35.75	   35.45-35.75</p>
<p>&quot;The market is calm and quiet as there is no fresh news. Levels are barely changed compared with the morning,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers saw current levels steady until the beginning of next year as banks were mainly closing positions and consolidating funds for 1997.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
